quadrf (1.0.6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Discover package-owned web application descriptors from apps.d and reuse
    each application's desktop Name, Comment and Icon in the control panel.
    The bundled radio apps ship their descriptor with quadrf-demos.
  * Show the Spatial RF Vision, Camera Decoder and PSD Plot desktop icons in
    the web Applications panel.
  * Move launcher entries and icons into the packages that own each app.
    The complete quadrf package depends on quadrf-gnuradio; quadrf-desktop
    no longer pulls quadrf-demos or GNU Radio.
  * Give the default demos reverse-DNS desktop IDs and AppStream metadata for
    standard software catalogs. Opt desktop icons in with
    X-QuadRF-Desktop=true; keep the old quadrf-* names; skip entries whose
    TryExec is missing.
  * Refresh the operator desktop automatically when packages install or remove
    launchers.
  * Switch wlan0 client, hotspot, or off from the control panel without a
    reboot. Persist the choice as QUADRF_WIFI_MODE. Saving a client SSID no
    longer reboots. QUADRF_WIFI_FALLBACK starts the hotspot after a failed
    client join without rewriting the saved mode.
  * The Network panel shows each path and which one served the browser.
  * Publish quadrf.local per interface and stop advertising avahi host
    records, wlan0 DHCP leases on the AP subnet, link-local, and loopback so
    a LAN client does not resolve to the hotspot.

 -- QuadRF Engineering <contact@ScaleRF.com>  Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:37:21 -0700

quadrf (1.0.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Per-install local HTTPS: generate a constrained CA and server
    certificate, serve platform-specific downloads, and use
    quadrf.local across connection modes. my.quadrf.com is gone.
